22 entries. Formalisable only on top of Tau Ceti or Mathlib main, which LeanBridge can use once its pins move forward; the work will then go into LeanBridge.

# Background › Algebraic geometry

* [`ag.plane_model`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Background/Algebraic-geometry/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_ag___plane_model_FLQQ_--statement) — Plane model. Difficulty: easy. Note: Done: builds on TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.projectivePlaneCurve, projectivePlaneCurve.smoothOfRelativeDimension and projectivePlaneCurve.functionFieldEquiv (Tau Ceti main), AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.BirationalOver (Mathlib) Missing: The definition itself: a plane curve G = 0 birational to X, called singular when G and its partial derivatives have a common zero over k̄. Roadmap: TauCetiRoadmap/AlgebraicCurves/README.md:969

# Background › Ring theory

* [`gl2.label`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Background/Ring-theory/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_gl2___label_FLQQ_--statement) — Label of a subgroup \$\\GL\_2(\\widehat\{\\Z\})\$. Difficulty: medium. GitHub issues: [#22](https://github.com/CBirkbeck/LeanBridge/issues/22). Note: Done: nothing formalised yet; builds on TauCeti.conreyCharacter (Tau Ceti main) and Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.adelicLevel, Matrix.GeneralLinearGroup.adelicGenus (LeanBridge) Missing: The RSZB tiebreaker n (the ordering of §2.4 of arXiv:2106.11141, to be transcribed) and, when det(H) ≠ Ẑ\^×, the prefix M.d.m ordering open subgroups of GL₁(Ẑ) by Conrey labels (TauCeti.conreyCharacter, Tau Ceti main).

# Groups › Lattices

* [`lattice.mass`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Groups/Lattices/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_lattice___mass_FLQQ_--statement) — Mass of a lattice. Difficulty: easy. Note: Done: nothing formalised yet; builds on TauCeti.IntegralLattice.genusClasses, TauCeti.IntegralLattice.IsPosDef.finite\_genusClasses (Tau Ceti main) and TauCeti.IntegralLattice.IsPosDef.finite\_isometry (Tau Ceti pin) Missing: The sum of 1/\#Aut(Λ) over Tau Ceti main's genusClasses (finite for definite lattices), using the pin's finiteness of isometry groups of definite lattices. Roadmap: TauCetiRoadmap/IntegralLattices/README.md:420
* [`lattice.pneighbor_adjacency`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Groups/Lattices/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_lattice___pneighbor_adjacency_FLQQ_--statement) — p-Neighbor adjacency matrix of a lattice. Difficulty: easy. Note: Done: nothing formalised yet; builds on TauCeti.IntegralLattice.IsNeighbor, TauCeti.IntegralLattice.genusClasses, TauCeti.IntegralLattice.IsometryQuotient (Tau Ceti main) Missing: The matrix indexed by Tau Ceti main's genusClasses whose (i, j) entry counts the p-neighbours of L\_i (IsNeighbor) isometric to L\_j, with finiteness of the set of p-neighbours.

# Modular forms › Classical

* [`cmf.eisenstein_label`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Modular-forms/Classical-modular-forms/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_cmf___eisenstein_label_FLQQ_--statement) — Label of a classical Eisenstein modular form. Difficulty: hard. GitHub issues: [#37](https://github.com/CBirkbeck/LeanBridge/issues/37). Note: Done: ModularForm.IsEisensteinNewform, DirichletCharacter.galoisOrbitIndex (LeanBridge); TauCeti.EisensteinSeries.normalizedCharG2MF, TauCeti.EisensteinSeries.weightedE1SIF, TauCeti.conreyCharacter (Tau Ceti main) Missing: Eisenstein newforms in weight 2 (from Tau Ceti main's weight-two series with character) and weight 1 (weighted weight-one series still to be proved modular), their Galois orbits ordered by trace sequences for the letter x, and the label N.k.E.a.x(.n.i) with Tau Ceti main's Conrey labels.
* [`cmf.eisenstein_newform`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Modular-forms/Classical-modular-forms/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_cmf___eisenstein_newform_FLQQ_--statement) — Eisenstein newform. Difficulty: medium. GitHub issues: [#37](https://github.com/CBirkbeck/LeanBridge/issues/37). Note: Done: ModularForm.IsEisensteinNewform, ModularForm.eisensteinFormsNew (LeanBridge, weight ≥ 3); TauCeti.EisensteinSeries.normalizedCharEisensteinSeriesMF (Tau Ceti); TauCeti.EisensteinSeries.normalizedCharG2MF, TauCeti.EisensteinSeries.weightedE1SIF (Tau Ceti main) Missing: Eisenstein newforms of weight 2 (Tau Ceti main's normalised weight-two series with character) and weight 1 (Tau Ceti main's weighted weight-one series, still to be proved modular), and the theorem that the Eisenstein newforms are a basis of E\_k\^new(N,χ). Roadmap: TauCetiRoadmap/ModularForms/README.md:305
* [`cmf.eisenstein_newspace`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Modular-forms/Classical-modular-forms/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_cmf___eisenstein_newspace_FLQQ_--statement) — New Eisenstein subspace. Difficulty: medium. GitHub issues: [#37](https://github.com/CBirkbeck/LeanBridge/issues/37). Note: Done: ModularForm.eisensteinFormsOld, ModularForm.eisensteinFormsNew, ModularForm.eisensteinFormsNewWeightTwo (LeanBridge); TauCeti.weightTwoEisensteinSubspace, TauCeti.EisensteinSeries.CharIndex.weightTwoForm (Tau Ceti main) Missing: E\_k\^new(N,χ) in weight 2 for every χ (spanned by Tau Ceti main's E₂\^\{χ₁,χ₂\}) and in weight 1 (weight-one series to be made modular), and the decomposition E\_k(N,χ) = E\_k\^old ⊕ E\_k\^new. Roadmap: TauCetiRoadmap/ModularForms/README.md:305
* [`cmf.embedding_label`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Modular-forms/Classical-modular-forms/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_cmf___embedding_label_FLQQ_--statement) — Complex embedding label. Difficulty: medium. GitHub issues: [#33](https://github.com/CBirkbeck/LeanBridge/issues/33). Note: Done: TauCeti.conreyCharacter, HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.labelPrefix (Tau Ceti main); HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.IsEmbedding, HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.galoisOrbitEmbedding, HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.coeffTrace (LeanBridge) Missing: The label N.k.a.x.c.j: the orbit letter x (as for cmf.label), c from Tau Ceti main's Conrey labelling of the nebentypus ι ∘ χ of ι(f), and j by the lexicographic order of (Re ι(aₙ), Im ι(aₙ))ₙ; that j ranges over all embeddings needs σ(f) to be a newform (issue \#38). Roadmap: TauCetiRoadmap/ModularForms/README.md:1020
* [`cmf.label`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Modular-forms/Classical-modular-forms/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_cmf___label_FLQQ_--statement) — Label of a classical modular form. Difficulty: medium. GitHub issues: [#33](https://github.com/CBirkbeck/LeanBridge/issues/33). Note: Done: TauCeti.NewformLabelPrefix, HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.labelPrefix, TauCeti.conreyCharacter (Tau Ceti main); HeckeRing.GL2.NewformOrbit, HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.coeffTrace (LeanBridge) Missing: The orbit letter x (base-26 position of the orbit's trace sequence in lexicographic order, over LeanBridge's NewformOrbit and coeffTrace), n from Tau Ceti main's Conrey labels and i from the embedding order; injectivity of x needs σ(f) to be a newform (issue \#38). Roadmap: TauCetiRoadmap/ModularForms/README.md:1020
* [`cmf.labels`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Modular-forms/Classical-modular-forms/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_cmf___labels_FLQQ_--statement) — Label of a classical modular form. Difficulty: hard. GitHub issues: [#33](https://github.com/CBirkbeck/LeanBridge/issues/33), [#37](https://github.com/CBirkbeck/LeanBridge/issues/37). Note: Done: HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.labelPrefix, TauCeti.conreyCharacter, TauCeti.weightTwoEisensteinSubspace (Tau Ceti main); ModularForm.IsEisensteinNewform, HeckeRing.GL2.NewformOrbit (LeanBridge) Missing: As cmf.label, plus the automorphic-type letter E/C, which needs Eisenstein newforms and their orbit labels in every weight (cmf.eisenstein\_label: weight 2 from Tau Ceti main's series, weight 1 still to be made modular). Roadmap: TauCetiRoadmap/ModularForms/README.md:1020
* [`cmf.minimal_twist`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Modular-forms/Classical-modular-forms/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_cmf___minimal_twist_FLQQ_--statement) — Minimal twist. Difficulty: medium. Note: Done: HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.IsTwistMinimal, HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.IsTwistBy, DirichletCharacter.IsMinimal (LeanBridge); HeckeRing.GL2.Newform.labelPrefix, TauCeti.conreyCharacter (Tau Ceti main) Missing: Once cmf labels exist (cmf.label, on Tau Ceti main), the twist of f with least label among its twist-minimal twists with minimal character; existence of such twists and the level formula lcm(N, cond ψ · cond χψ) are theorems.

# Representations › Dirichlet characters

* [`character.dirichlet.conrey.conductor`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Representations/Dirichlet-characters/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_character___dirichlet___conrey___conductor_FLQQ_--statement) — Conductor of a Dirichlet character from its Conrey label. Difficulty: medium. GitHub issues: [#13](https://github.com/CBirkbeck/LeanBridge/issues/13). Note: Missing: The conductor of chi\_q(n,·) from n on top of TauCeti.conreyCharacter: it is the product over the prime-power factors, with the explicit conductors at odd p (order of n\^(p-1)) and at p = 2.
* [`character.dirichlet.conrey.parity`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Representations/Dirichlet-characters/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_character___dirichlet___conrey___parity_FLQQ_--statement) — Parity of a Dirichlet character from its Conrey label. Difficulty: easy. GitHub issues: [#13](https://github.com/CBirkbeck/LeanBridge/issues/13). Note: Missing: The parity criterion for TauCeti.conreyCharacter: chi\_\{p\^e\}(n,·) is even iff n is a square mod p (mod 4 for p = 2, e \> 1), and parity is additive over the prime-power factors.

# Varieties › Abelian varieties over 𝔽\_q

* [`av.fq.newton_elevation`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Abelian-varieties-over-Fq/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_av___fq___newton_elevation_FLQQ_--statement) — Newton polygon elevation. Difficulty: medium. Note: Done: builds on Polynomial.newtonPolygon, Polynomial.newtonSlopes and Polynomial.newtonPolygon\_reverse (Tau Ceti main), Polynomial.IsWeilPolynomial (LeanBridge) Missing: Eligible polygons, their elevation and partial order (pure combinatorics), and 'almost ordinary' through the Newton polygon of the L-polynomial for v\_p / v\_p(q).
* [`av.fq.supersingular`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Abelian-varieties-over-Fq/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_av___fq___supersingular_FLQQ_--statement) — Supersingular abelian variety. Difficulty: easy. GitHub issues: [#66](https://github.com/CBirkbeck/LeanBridge/issues/66). Note: Done: builds on Polynomial.newtonSlopes and Polynomial.newtonSlopes\_reverse (Tau Ceti main), Polynomial.IsWeilPolynomial (LeanBridge) Missing: Supersingular Weil q-polynomials (every Newton slope of the reverse, for v\_p / v\_p(q), equal to 1/2); for an abelian variety, its Weil polynomial (av.fq.weil\_polynomial).

# Varieties › Belyi maps

* [`belyi.base_field`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Belyi-maps/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_belyi___base_field_FLQQ_--statement) — Base field of a Belyi map. Difficulty: medium. Note: Done: builds on TauCeti.IsAlgebraicBelyiPair and IsAlgebraicBelyiPair.of\_mapRingEquiv (Tau Ceti main), AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.fieldsOfDefinition (LeanBridge) Missing: Fields of definition and the field of moduli of an algebraic Belyi pair over ℚ̄ (the database takes the field of moduli whenever it is a field of definition). Roadmap: TauCetiRoadmap/BelyiMaps/README.md:3616
* [`belyi.num_orbits`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Belyi-maps/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_belyi___num_orbits_FLQQ_--statement) — Number of Galois orbits. Difficulty: hard. Note: Done: builds on TauCeti.IsAlgebraicBelyiPair.of\_mapRingEquiv and TauCeti.AnalyticBelyiPair.isoClassEquivConnectedIsoClass (Tau Ceti main), TauCeti.PassportSpec.classSet (Tau Ceti pin) Missing: The Galois action on isomorphism classes of algebraic Belyi pairs over ℚ̄, algebraic passports, and the number of orbits in a passport. Roadmap: TauCetiRoadmap/BelyiMaps/README.md:3605
* [`belyi.orbit_size`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Belyi-maps/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_belyi___orbit_size_FLQQ_--statement) — Orbit size. Difficulty: medium. Note: Done: builds on TauCeti.IsAlgebraicBelyiPair and IsAlgebraicBelyiPair.of\_mapRingEquiv (Tau Ceti main), TauCeti.PassportSpec.passportSize and TauCeti.ConnectedIsoClass (Tau Ceti pin) Missing: Isomorphism classes of algebraic Belyi pairs over ℚ̄ with the Galois action by conjugation, and the cardinalities of the orbits. Roadmap: TauCetiRoadmap/BelyiMaps/README.md:3725
* [`belyi.ramification_type`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Belyi-maps/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_belyi___ramification_type_FLQQ_--statement) — Ramification type. Difficulty: easy. Note: Done: builds on TauCeti.Place.markedPlace (Tau Ceti main) and TauCeti.Place.ramificationIdx (Tau Ceti pin); analytic analogue TauCeti.TopBranchedCover.ramificationPartition with TauCeti.AnalyticBelyiPair.toTopBranchedCover (Tau Ceti main) Missing: The triple of partitions of an algebraic Belyi pair: e(P) repeated deg P times over the places above t = 0, 1, ∞. Roadmap: TauCetiRoadmap/BelyiMaps/README.md:2880

# Varieties › Elliptic curves

* [`ec.q.faltings_ratio`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Elliptic-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_ec___q___faltings_ratio_FLQQ_--statement) — Faltings ratio. Difficulty: hard. GitHub issues: [#26](https://github.com/CBirkbeck/LeanBridge/issues/26). Note: Done: builds on the Néron lattice of ec.q.period\_lattice (Waiting for bump, from PeriodPair.weierstrassCurve on Tau Ceti main) and WeierstrassCurve.isogenyClass, WeierstrassCurve.faltingsHeight, WeierstrassCurve.periodCovolume (LeanBridge) Missing: The Néron lattice of a curve over ℚ (complex uniformisation), then the index in it of the Néron lattice of the curve of the isogeny class whose lattice lies in all the others.
* [`ec.q.period_lattice`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Elliptic-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_ec___q___period_lattice_FLQQ_--statement) — Period lattice of an elliptic curve. Difficulty: hard. GitHub issues: [#26](https://github.com/CBirkbeck/LeanBridge/issues/26). Note: Done: builds on PeriodPair.weierstrassCurve and PeriodPair.weierstrassPoint (Tau Ceti main), WeierstrassCurve.exists\_variableChange\_of\_j\_eq (Mathlib); the real period is WeierstrassCurve.realPeriod (Tau Ceti pin) and the covolume WeierstrassCurve.periodCovolume (LeanBridge) Missing: The converse uniformisation (every elliptic curve over ℂ is some E\_Λ, with Λ fixed by the invariant differential), hence the period lattice of a Weierstrass equation and the Néron lattice of its reduced minimal model.

# Varieties › Genus 2 curves

* [`g2c.tame_reduction`](https://cbirkbeck.github.io/LeanBridge/Varieties/Genus-2-curves/#--informal-preview-_FLQQ_g2c___tame_reduction_FLQQ_--statement) — Tame reduction. Difficulty: medium. Note: Done: ingredients only: TauCeti.HasNodalReduction (Tau Ceti main), TauCeti.IsTamelyRamified (Tau Ceti pin) Missing: The predicate that semistable reduction is attained after a finite tamely ramified extension, on top of Tau Ceti main's HasNodalReduction and Tau Ceti's IsTamelyRamified; the bound p \> 2g + 1 is a further theorem that needs stable reduction.
